---
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is SORBS?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'The Spam and Open Relay Blocking System, a blocklist family covering spam sources, dynamic IPs, and exploited hosts. Some mail admins weight it heavily.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How long does SORBS delisting take?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Requests are processed manually and can take days. SORBS also asks for a donation consideration on some listing classes, unlike Spamhaus.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Why was I listed without sending spam?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Dynamic IP ranges and shared hosts get listed because of other tenants or a past assignment. The fix is proving a static, clean source or moving to one.' } },
  ],
};
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

---
<BaseLayout title="How to Get Delisted from SORBS" description="SORBS delisting guide: how SORBS listings work, the escalation timer, and the request process that actually works."  
 breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["Email Authentication", "/email-authentication/"], ["Email Deliverability", "/email-deliverability/"], ["SORBS Delisting"]]}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-deliverability/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Deliverability</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">SORBS Delisting</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Get Delisted from SORBS</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      SORBS (Spam and Open-Relay Blocking System) lists IPs for spam-sending behavior, open relays,
      and related abuse. It is best known for one policy quirk: new IPs and some listings carry an
      automatic timeout, but requesting removal incorrectly can extend the wait.
    </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>How SORBS listings behave</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Many zones auto-expire (typically 48 hours to days) if the trigger stops.</li>
        <li>Open-relay and exploit listings require proof of fix, not just time.</li>
        <li>Requests from IPs that are still sending spam extend or re-list.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>The working procedure</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li><strong>Confirm the listing and zone</strong> via the <a href="/blacklist-checker/">blacklist checker</a> or SORBS's own lookup (public-resolver queries may be refused).</li>
        <li><strong>Stop the trigger</strong>: compromised account, open relay/proxy, spam run, or abused web form.</li>
        <li><strong>Fix the posture</strong>: <a href="/spf-record-checker/">SPF</a>, <a href="/dkim-record-checker/">DKIM</a>, <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/">DMARC</a>, correct PTR, no direct sending from dynamic space.</li>
        <li><strong>Submit one delisting request</strong> through the SORBS interface with a real explanation and the fix description.</li>
        <li><strong>Respect the timer.</strong> If the listing carries an automatic expiry inside your window, waiting is often faster than requesting.</li>
      </ol>
      
<h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is SORBS?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The Spam and Open Relay Blocking System, a blocklist family covering spam sources, dynamic IPs, and exploited hosts. Some mail admins weight it heavily.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does SORBS delisting take?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Requests are processed manually and can take days. SORBS also asks for a donation consideration on some listing classes, unlike Spamhaus.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why was I listed without sending spam?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Dynamic IP ranges and shared hosts get listed because of other tenants or a past assignment. The fix is proving a static, clean source or moving to one.</p></details></div>
      <h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/remove-from-spamhaus-blocklist/">Spamhaus removal</a> and <a href="/get-off-barracuda-blocklist/">Barracuda removal</a></li>
        <li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/">Why emails go to spam</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
